==Trivia==
*The number of possible [[Battle Decks|decks]] that can be created with 2 evolutions is 28, assuming that all 8 [[cards]] in the deck can evolve.
*The [[Ice Spirit/Evolution|Ice Spirit]] and [[Bats/Evolution|Bats]] are the only evolutions without a purple diamond being represented on their card renders.
*The [[Battle Ram/Evolution|Battle Ram]] is the only evolution to spawn another evolved troop as a part of its mechanics.
*The [[Skeletons/Evolution|Skeletons]] and [[Ice Spirit/Evolution|Ice Spirit]] are the cheapest evolutions and require the least amount Elixir to fully cycle, costing 1 [[Elixir]] alone and 3 Elixir when fully cycled (excluding Elixir spent from playing other cards).
*The [[P.E.K.K.A./Evolution|P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Royal Recruits/Evolution|Royal Recruits]], and [[Mega Knight/Evolution|Mega Knight]] are the costliest evolutions, costing 7 Elixir alone.
*The [[Royal Hogs/Evolution|Royal Hogs]] require the most amount of Elixir to fully cycle, costing 15 Elixir when fully cycled (excluding Elixir spent from playing other cards).
*The [[Barbarians/Evolution|Barbarians]] were the first evolution to be fully revealed.
*Some [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] and [[:Category:Building Cards|buildings]] resemble Super Troops from Clash of Clans. More specifically:
**The Evolved Barbarians resemble the Super Barbarian.
**The [[Cannon/Evolution|Evolved Cannon]] resembles the Eagle Artillery.
**The [[Valkyrie/Evolution|Evolved Valkyrie]] resembles the Super Valkyrie.
**The [[Witch/Evolution|Evolved Witch]] resembles the Super Witch.
**The [[Wizard/Evolution|Evolved Wizard]] resembles the Super Wizard.
*The [[Bomber/Evolution|Evolved Bomber]]'s ability is the same mechanic as the one used by the Bomber from the Clash of Clans Builder Base.
*The P.E.K.K.A. and Mega Knight's abilities resemble old upgrades from Clash Mini.
*The [[Elite Barbarians/Evolution|Elite Barbarians]]' abilities are based on the the common modifier in [[C.H.A.O.S.]].
*Card Evolutions do not have alternative skins that take [[Star Points]]. This can be seen with the [[Skeleton Barrel/Evolution|Evolved Skeleton Barrel]]; the Skeletons spawned on death will not show a Star Level.
*All Card Evolutions are 3-D models when deployed into the arena. This is different from the 2-D sprites used in their regular forms.
**The only exception to this rule is the Ice Spirit, which re-uses its base form's sprite, except that it now has a purple tint.

